---
import SectionTitle from "~/components/security/SectionTitle.astro"
import SquaredGrid from "./SquaredGrid.astro"
---

<section class="how-it-works">
    <SquaredGrid />
    <div class="container">
        <SectionTitle title="How it works">
            It takes three steps, all on your machine.
        </SectionTitle>

        <ol>
            <li>
                <div>
                    <span class="step">1</span>
                    <h3>Export</h3>
                    <p>
                        A vRO administrator exports a .package from the
                        Orchestrator client. If vRA starts your workflows,
                        export the vRA content from VMware Build Tools as well,
                        so the brief can see what triggers them. Put both in one
                        folder.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <pre><code>my-estate/
<span class="muted">├─</span> lb-usecase.package
<span class="muted">└─</span> vra-export/</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>
                <div>
                    <span class="step">2</span>
                    <h3>Run</h3>
                    <p>
                        The first time, init creates a config file in your home
                        folder where you choose your model and settings. Then
                        run sanitizes the export, maps every workflow and the
                        systems it touches, and writes the brief to a
                        kestra-assessment folder next to the exports.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <pre><code><span class="muted">$</span> kestra-migrate init
<span class="muted">$</span> kestra-migrate vra run ./my-estate</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>
                <div>
                    <span class="step">3</span>
                    <h3>Answer and run again</h3>
                    <p>
                        When the exports can't answer something, such as how
                        often a workflow runs or what else starts it, the tool
                        writes the question to answers.yaml, with a suggested
                        answer where the code points to one. Fill in the answers
                        and run the same command again. When there are no open
                        questions left, the plan is final.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <pre><code class="yaml"><span class="muted">-</span> <span class="key">id</span><span class="muted">:</span> auth.avi-controller
  <span class="key">question</span><span class="muted">:</span> How do the flows sign in to Avi?
  <span class="key">suggested</span><span class="muted">:</span> <span class="answer">basic authentication, as today</span></code></pre>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
    @use "/src/components/vra-migration-guide/shared" as *;

    // Figma's code-block values; they stay dark in both themes.
    $code-value: #f7f7f8;
    $code-answer: #80fac5;

    .how-it-works {
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
        @include assistant-section(var(--ks-background-secondary));
    }

    .container {
        @include guide-container;
    }

    ol {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: 1rem;
        margin: 1rem 0 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;

        @include media-breakpoint-up(xl) {
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
        }
    }

    li {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 2rem;
        padding: 2rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--ks-border-primary);
        border-radius: $border-radius-lg;
        background: var(--ks-background-body);
        box-shadow: $calc-shadow-surface;

        > div {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: flex-start;
            gap: 0.5rem;
        }

        p {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 1rem;
            line-height: 1.5rem;
        }
    }

    .step {
        padding: 0.125rem 0.5rem;
        border-radius: 6px;
        background: color-mix(
            in srgb,
            var(--blue-300) 10%,
            var(--ks-background-body)
        );
        font-size: $font-size-sm;
        font-weight: 600;
        line-height: 1.25rem;
        color: var(--blue-400);

        :global(html.dark) & {
            color: var(--blue-300);
        }
    }

    h3 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: $font-size-2xl;
        font-weight: 600;
        line-height: 2.375rem;
    }

    pre {
        min-height: 105px;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 1rem;
        overflow-x: auto;
        border-radius: $border-radius-lg;
        background: $dark-bg-input;
    }

    code {
        padding: 0;
        background: none;
        font-family: $font-family-monospace;
        font-size: $font-size-xs;
        line-height: 1.5rem;
        white-space: pre;
        color: $white;
    }

    .muted {
        color: $dark-text-muted;
    }

    .yaml {
        color: $code-value;
    }

    .key {
        color: $dark-link;
    }

    .answer {
        color: $code-answer;
    }
</style>
